# Reference: Testing — Scenarios, Parity, Non-functional

## Scenario suite (run from NetX UI and Wove UI; results must match)
| ID | Scenario | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| S01 | Single-account buy, shares, market, DAY | 1 order; identical fields both channels |
| S02 | Buy in dollars (fractional or rounded per firm rule) | Server-computed quantity identical |
| S03 | Sell-all of a position with pending sell | Holdings validation nets pending order |
| S04 | Limit order outside price collar | WARNING, ack required, then submittable |
| S05 | Restricted security | ERROR, submit blocked |
| S06 | Insufficient buying power | ERROR with amount shortfall |
| S07 | Mutual fund exchange within family | Correct pairing of sell/buy lines |
| S08 | Multi-account worksheet, 50 lines | All lines validated; per-line messages |
| S09 | Model rebalance generate | Backend-generated lines identical from both UIs |
| S10 | Block order, pro-rata allocation with residual | Allocation + residual rule applied |
| S11 | Submit requiring supervisory approval | PENDING_APPROVAL → approve in other UI → submitted |
| S12 | Double-click / network retry on submit | One set of orders (idempotency) |
| S13 | Concurrent edit NetX vs Wove | Second write gets 409; UI reload flow works |
| S14 | Edit after validation | Status returns to DRAFT; submit blocked until revalidated |
| S15 | Stale validation (> N sec) at submit | 422 WS_STALE_VALIDATION |
| S16 | User without entitlement to one account on the worksheet | 403; no partial leakage of data |
| S17 | Wove kill switch on | Wove read-only; NetX unaffected |
| S18 | Compliance engine down | 503 WS_DOWNSTREAM_UNAVAILABLE; nothing submitted |
| S19 | Partial submit failure (routing rejects 1 line) | Per-line status; others unaffected |
| S20 | After market close, DAY order | Rejected or queued per firm rule, same in both |

## Parity harness
- Drive scenarios through the API with `X-Channel` set to NETX and WOVE (and through the old NetX path during Phase 3).
- Capture the generated orders at the routing boundary (stub/record) rather than in the UI.
- Diff field by field; allow-list only fields that are expected to differ (channel, timestamps, IDs).
- Run in CI on every change to the facade, worksheet service, or either UI's worksheet module.

## Test layers
- **Backend:** unit (validation, state machine), contract (from OpenAPI), integration (DB, Kafka outbox, idempotency store), security (authz per route, IDOR).
- **UI:** component tests on the shared client mocks; Playwright e2e per scenario for both UIs against a seeded test environment.
- **Consumer-driven contracts (e.g. Pact):** Wove and NetX UI as consumers of the facade.

## Non-functional checklist
- [ ] p95 latency: validate and submit within SLO for max-size worksheet
- [ ] Load: N concurrent users, M-line worksheets, no lock contention deadlocks
- [ ] Idempotency store TTL ≥ max client retry window; survives node restart
- [ ] Outbox: no lost or duplicate events on broker outage (consumers dedupe on eventId)
- [ ] SSE/WebSocket: reconnect with last-seen version; entitlement-filtered stream
- [ ] Audit: every command recorded with channel, user, before/after, correlation ID; retention meets policy
- [ ] Logs redact account numbers / PII per policy
- [ ] Authz: every route checks entitlement server-side; tested with a user of another office
- [ ] Input limits: max lines, payload size, rate limiting per user
- [ ] Kill switch and feature flags tested in production-like env
- [ ] Dashboards + alerts live before pilot
- [ ] Rollback rehearsed for each phase
